WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
It is time for Drew's News.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.530
The only news that feels like finding

3
00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:08.410
a four leaf clover every day, hopefully.

4
00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:12.320
And with me at the desk, my little shamrock, Ross Matthews.

5
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.253
Hi, everybody. Hi.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.421
Happy Saint Patrick's day.

7
00:00:17.421 --> 00:00:19.200
It is Saint Patrick's day

8
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.900
so I guess I can't pinch you Rossi,

9
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.100
because you're wearing green.

10
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.910
I am wearing green and look, I have a beard.

11
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.290
I haven't had a beard since high school.

12
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.815
She was a sweet girl.

13
00:00:28.815 --> 00:00:31.106
(Drew laughs)

14
00:00:31.106 --> 00:00:32.280
I bet she was, Rossi.

15
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.540
Look at that.

16
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:34.651
Hi, everybody.

17
00:00:34.651 --> 00:00:35.990
(audience applauds)

18
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:38.010
Happy Saint Patrick's day, everyone.

19
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.750
Now 54% of adults are celebrating today.

20
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.290
And Rossi, guess economically speaking

21
00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.800
how much money people are spending on this holiday?

22
00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.310
I have no idea.

23
00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.520
Hold on to your leprechaun hat, Rossi,

24
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.560
because Martha Stewart Magazine reports

25
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:56.420
that people will spend $5.87 billion.

26
00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:57.420
What? What?

27
00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.760
So I'm like, what?

28
00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.430 line:15%
It's a lot of, you know,

29
00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:04.280 line:15%
alcohol, and shamrock shakes, and bar business.

30
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.990 line:15%
And listen, this is good for the economy.

31
00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.810 line:15%
The average person will spend about 42 bucks

32
00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:13.470 line:15%
on everything from green clothes, to corned beef,

33
00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.760 line:15%
and green beer.

34
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.330 line:15%
So hey, happy Saint Patrick's day

35
00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.270 line:15%
and happy boost to the economy.

36
00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:20.733
Well, yeah, I think...

37
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:23.040
(audience applauds)

38
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.150
5.7 billion seems like a lot,

39
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.620
but when you break it down to like $42,

40
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.980
yeah, like I bought this green shirt.

41
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.040
I didn't have a green shirt,

42
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.190
but I knew I wanted to wear a green shirt, you know?

43
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.660
I love the color of that green.

44
00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.620
It's got a lot of blue and it's very attractive.

45
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.490
Thank you. Thank you.

46
00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.746
All right, hey, next up, anyone here watch "Fleabag"

47
00:01:38.746 --> 00:01:40.998
with Phoebe Waller-Bridge?

48
00:01:40.998 --> 00:01:42.665
(audience applauds)

49
00:01:42.665 --> 00:01:44.640
Well, if you love that show, great news.

50
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.090
Hollywood Reporter says Amazon just green lit...

51
00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.480
Green lit on Saint Patrick's day.

52
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.880
Green lit her next series.

53
00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.550
Details are under wraps a little bit,

54
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.970
but it shoots later this year.

55
00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.420 line:15%
And remember, "Fleabag" premiered on Amazon

56
00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.700 line:15%
way back in 2016, and it cleaned up at the Emmy's.

57
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.730 line:15%
It won six of 'em.

58
00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:03.260 line:15%
And since then, Phoebe has been super busy.

59
00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.780 line:15%
She launched "Killing Eve," which I'm obsessed with,

60
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:06.960 line:15%
with Sandra Oh.

61
00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.960 line:15%
She co-wrote the latest Bond movie.

62
00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.180 line:15%
And now she stars opposite Harrison Ford

63
00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.046
in Indiana Jones five.

64
00:02:13.046 --> 00:02:13.879
(Drew gasps)

65
00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:14.712
I know. I know.

66
00:02:14.712 --> 00:02:16.370
And she has a brand new project coming.

67
00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.970
She really is the cat's pajamas.

68
00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:19.870
Yeah, she is.

69
00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.550
I cannot wait to see the show.

70
00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.130
I need Phoebe Waller-Bridge.

71
00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.210
I'm on the feeder.

72
00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.640
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

73
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.907
Yeah, yeah, uh-huh, I could.

74
00:02:27.907 --> 00:02:31.110
I started it, and then I just watched

75
00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.190
too much "90 Day Fiance."

76
00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.830
It's like everything else just gets back seat.

77
00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.980
Do yourself a favor, Rossi,

78
00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.130
and get on the "Fleabag" thing.

79
00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.910
God, it's just so good.

80
00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:41.967
Okay, I'm sold.

81
00:02:41.967 --> 00:02:45.134 line:15%
(upbeat bright music)

